The SDIO product table has the CYW43455 only under 0xa9bf. The chip on a
Raspberry Pi 5 Model B Rev 1.0 (d04170) reports 02d0:4345 in its CIS, so
sdmmc leaves all three functions "not configured" and there is no bwfm0.
The firmware is chosen afterwards by the chip's ID and revision, not by
this number. OpenBSD's if_bwfm_sdio.c matches SDMMC_PRODUCT_BROADCOM_BCM4345
in the same way.

--- a/sys/dev/sdmmc/if_bwfm_sdio.c
+++ b/sys/dev/sdmmc/if_bwfm_sdio.c
@@ -305,6 +305,11 @@
 		SDMMC_PRODUCT_BROADCOM_BCM43455,
 		SDMMC_CIS_BROADCOM_BCM43455
 	},
+	{
+		SDMMC_VENDOR_BROADCOM,
+		SDMMC_PRODUCT_BROADCOM_BCM4345,
+		SDMMC_CIS_BROADCOM_BCM4345
+	},
 	{
 		SDMMC_VENDOR_BROADCOM,
 		SDMMC_PRODUCT_BROADCOM_BCM43362,
